# ESP32 4x4 Keypad + OLED Display

This project demonstrates a simple **keypad typing interface** on an **ESP32** using a **4x4 matrix keypad** and an **SSD1306 128×64 OLED display**.  
Every key you press appears on the screen in real time. The buffer automatically scrolls to keep the most recent characters visible.  
Supported keys: `0–9`, `A–D`, `#`, and `*`.

---

## 🧭 Features
- Displays typed keypad input on a 128×64 OLED screen  
- Automatically wraps and scrolls long text  
- Ignores invalid keys (e.g., none detected)  
- Uses I²C for OLED and digital pins for keypad matrix

---

## ⚙️ Wiring Diagram

### OLED Display (SSD1306 I²C)
| OLED Pin | ESP32 Pin | Description |
|-----------|------------|-------------|
| VCC       | 3.3V       | Power supply |
| GND       | GND        | Ground |
| SDA       | 21         | I²C data |
| SCL       | 22         | I²C clock |

### 4x4 Keypad
| Keypad Pin | ESP32 GPIO | Role |
|-------------|-------------|------|
| R1 | 14 | Row 1 |
| R2 | 12 | Row 2 |
| R3 | 13 | Row 3 |
| R4 | 4  | Row 4 *(changed from 15 to avoid boot issues)* |
| C1 | 32 | Column 1 |
| C2 | 33 | Column 2 |
| C3 | 25 | Column 3 |
| C4 | 26 | Column 4 |

---

## 🧩 Dependencies (PlatformIO)
```ini
lib_deps =
  adafruit/Adafruit SSD1306@^2.5.10
  adafruit/Adafruit GFX Library@^1.11.11
  adafruit/Adafruit BusIO@^1.16.2
  Chris--A/Keypad@^3.1.1
